 "fig2_title": "Partial-credit reward climbs for every format, but what it climbs toward is copying the input",
 "fig3_title": "Partial-credit RL lifts the score at every length, only up to what a verbatim copy earns (~25%)",
 "fig4_title": "Per-base errors sit at chance (~75%) at token edges and inside tokens: no skill, so no boundary effect",
 "fig7_title": "Input compression barely matters once the policy copies: every format sits near the 25% copy score",
 "fig8_title": "Exact-match reward: 0 of 4,568 reverse-complement rollouts were correct, so GRPO had no gradient",
 "fig9_title": "Partial-credit RL taught the model to copy the DNA instead of reverse-complementing it",
 "tldr": [
  "<strong>Exact-match reward gives no learning signal.</strong> 0 of 4,568 reverse-complement training rollouts were correct in any format, so every GRPO group had zero variance and zero gradient.",
  "<strong>Partial-credit reward gets gamed.</strong> The policy learned to copy the input verbatim: 88% (raw), 98% (per-base), 74% (6-mer) of answers after RL, up from 8%, 17% and 5%. A copy always has the right length and scores ~25% by chance.",
  "<strong>The format changed how faithfully the model copies, not whether it can reverse-complement.</strong> Errors sit at chance (~75% per base) at token edges and inside tokens alike.",
  "<strong>A DNA-trained model has the skill, and its errors follow its tokenizer.</strong> Carbon-X reverse-complements 68.5% of the same prompts exactly, counts GC right only ~10%, and drops from ~80% to 44% accuracy as its padded leftover 6-mer chunk grows."
 ],
 "fig10_title": "Copying takes over between steps 20 and 50 of partial-credit training; the exact-match run never moves",
 "fig11_title": "A DNA-trained model has the skill: Carbon-X reverse-complements 68% exactly where Qwen3-0.6B gets 0%, yet counts GC right only ~10%",
 "fig12_title": "Carbon-X errors are rare once the length is right; most of its failures are length errors",
 "fig13_title": "Carbon-X stumbles on a long leftover chunk: 77\u201383% exact with 0\u20132 letters left over, 44% with 5",
